  "description": "Follow-up from TASK-7.14 (doc-111). Many postflop golden spots reach their decision through hero preflop actions the project's own chart grades as Major errors (e.g. UTG opening 92o, 82o, T4o, K3o, K2o; CO opening 72o, 83o; full-ring UTG 94o; BB only calling an SB raise with AA) \u2014 code review MINOR hero-preflop-lines-contradict-chart. A trainer's reference spots should not model bad preflop play. Also: 6max-turn-bb-raise-92o says 'set of kings' where it means kings full; and a gradeDecision RangeError escapes parsePostflopGoldenSpots instead of being reported as a problem (NIT grade-throw-escapes-validation).",
